<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani bourse market capitalisation falls.</title>
<headline>Pakistani bourse market capitalisation falls.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange said on Friday its listed firms market capitalisation fell to 499.455 billion rupees in March from 527.167 billion in February. Following are the details:</p>
<p>						March	February</p>
<p>Listed capital (in billion rupees)  204.126    203.347</p>
<p>Market capitalisation (in billion)  499.455    527.167</p>
<p>Turnover of shares (in million)     936.593    874.628</p>
<p>KSE 100 index  (points)	     1,574.70   1,667.05</p>
<p>KSE all share index (points)	1,014.79   1,071.74</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
